 {
  "sha": "ee202a64f60b0f211485c2f3dfb08ba3b33433ee",
  "node_id": "C_kwDOSVZ-Q9oAKGVlMjAyYTY0ZjYwYjBmMjExNDg1YzJmM2RmYjA4YmEzYjMzNDMzZWU",
  "commit": {
   "author": {
    "name": "Kody Wildfeuer",
    "email": "kwildfeuer@me.com",
    "date": "2026-08-28T02:30:39Z"
   },
   "committer": {
    "name": "Kody Wildfeuer",
    "email": "kwildfeuer@me.com",
    "date": "2026-08-28T02:30:39Z"
   },
   "message": "pages: Article XXIV compliance \u2014 classic.html reads CI-harvested static GitHub snapshot, never api.github.com\n\nclassic.html's card, egg-seal, agent chips, mutation log, fork count, and\nparent-lineage-gift paths all called api.github.com live, unauthenticated,\nfrom the visitor's browser (self-referential: owner/repo derived from\nlocation.host/pathname at view time). Now scripts/harvest_gh_snapshot.py\n(run by .github/workflows/build-gh-snapshot.yml on push + daily schedule)\nharvests self repo metadata, recent commits, and the agents/ contents\nlisting, plus \u2014 for older seeds without a baked-in lineage_snapshot \u2014 the\nsame three signals for rappid.json's parent_repo, into state/*.json in the\nidentical API response shapes. Each call site changed by URL only; parsing\nuntouched. The one remaining api.github.com call (viewer-is-operator check)\nis authenticated with a Bearer token and stays live by design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
